From: Khem Raj <khem.raj@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] testlib: Use a local label in the riscv32 cycle counter

The 32-bit RISC-V getticks() loops on a named "start" label in inline
assembly. getticks() is an inline function, so where it is expanded
more than once in a translation unit the label is defined several
times, and the clang integrated assembler rejects it:

  src/testlib/3rdparty/cycle/cycle_p.h:587:17: error: symbol 'start' is already defined

Use a local numeric label instead, which can be redefined.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Khem Raj <khem.raj@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/testlib/3rdparty/cycle/cycle_p.h | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/src/testlib/3rdparty/cycle/cycle_p.h
+++ b/src/testlib/3rdparty/cycle/cycle_p.h
@@ -584,11 +584,11 @@
   asm volatile("rdtime %0" : "=r" (result));
 #elif __riscv_xlen == 32
   uint32_t l, h, h2;
-  asm volatile(	"start:\n"
+  asm volatile(	"1:\n"
 		"rdtimeh %0\n"
 		"rdtime %1\n"
 		"rdtimeh %2\n"
-		"bne %0, %2, start\n"
+		"bne %0, %2, 1b\n"
 		: "=r" (h), "=r" (l), "=r" (h2));
   result = (((uint64_t)h)<<32) | ((uint64_t)l);
 #else
